<p>
This course is accelerated!  That means it moves at more than double the pace of a normal semester.  The reality is that to be successful, several hours a day will need to be dedicated to your studies.  Studying on weekends to get ahead, especially if holding a job or other commitments during the work week, will be helpful.  Below is a table with time you might expect to spend on each aspect of the course (for each section of the textbook).  Note that this totals roughly 4 hours per day or 20 hours per week!  In reality, this is likely the bare minimum you should expect to spend working on this course each week.  
</p>

